# VibrationFit Core Conventions

## Feature Registry

Before modifying Life Vision, Token System, Design System, or Database Schema, check `FEATURE_REGISTRY.md` in the project root:

- LOCKED = do not modify without explicit user permission
- STABLE = modify with caution, test the entire feature afterward
- IN PROGRESS = safe to modify

## File Placement

| What | Where |
|------|-------|
| Documentation | `docs/[category]/` — NEVER in project root |
| Database files, schema docs | `supabase/` |
| Migrations | `supabase/migrations/YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_description.sql`, apply via Supabase MCP `execute_sql` |
| Components | `src/components/` (PascalCase) |
| Utilities | `src/lib/` (kebab-case) |
| AI prompts | `src/lib/viva/prompts/` only — never inline in API routes |
| Temp/debug files | `temp/` (gitignored) |
| One-off scripts | `scripts/[category]/`, move to `scripts/archive/` after a successful run |

Schema source of truth: `supabase/COMPLETE_SCHEMA_DUMP.sql`. Never auto-update it after a migration; the user regenerates it. Never reference `supabase/archive/`.

## Brand Voice & Terminology

- NEVER use "AI" in user-facing text — always "VIVA" (e.g. "VIVA Coach", "Powered by VIVA"). Technical names like `AIButton` may keep "AI".
- Say "Actualize" not "Complete", "Vision" not "Goal", "Alignment" not "Progress"
- "Above the Green Line" = aligned/success states; "Below the Green Line" = contrast/awareness
- NO emojis in code or UI text — use Lucide React icons (`lucide-react`)
